<header class="site-header">
  <a class="site-brand" href="/" aria-label="YoYoCoyote home">
    <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">Y</span>
    <span><strong>YoYoCoyote</strong><small>REGION OF WATERLOO</small></span>
  </a>
  <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
    <a href="/">Map</a>
    {{#if user}}
      <a href="/reports">My reports</a>
      <form action="/logout" method="post">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{csrfToken}}">
        <button type="submit" class="nav-action">Log out</button>
      </form>
    {{else}}
      <a href="/login">Log in</a>
      <a href="/signup" class="nav-signup">Create account</a>
    {{/if}}
  </nav>
</header>

<main class="container about-page">
  <section class="about-intro">
    <div class="about-intro-copy">
      <p class="about-kicker">A COMMUNITY WILDLIFE PROJECT</p>
      <h1>Sharing the landscape with coyotes.</h1>
      <p class="about-lede">
        YoYoCoyote brings community-reported sightings together on a map of the Region of Waterloo, helping build a
        clearer picture of local coyote activity.
      </p>
      <a class="about-cta" href="/">Explore the sightings map <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="about-image">
      <img src="/coyote.jpg" alt="A coyote standing and looking toward the camera">
      <figcaption>One shared map. Many community observations.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <p class="about-kicker">HOW IT WORKS</p>
    <h2>Reports from the people who live here.</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone can report a sighting from the map, with or without an account. Reports are gathered in one place so
      visitors can see community observations across the region. An account links your reports to you and gives you a
      personal list to revisit.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section about-purpose">
    <p class="about-kicker">THE PROJECT'S PURPOSE</p>
    <h2>Better understanding through shared observations.</h2>
    <p>
      As described in the project README, YoYoCoyote aims to support conservation, education, and safety for people and
      coyotes alike. The README also states that collected information is intended to be shared with the Region of
      Waterloo, the University of Waterloo, Wilfrid Laurier University, and the University of Guelph.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="about-note">Community sightings are observations, not emergency reports or official wildlife guidance.</p>
</main>